  "highlight": "Barbara Pellick crossed the English Channel from England to France in 12 hours 23 minutes on 4 July 1995.",
  "biography": [
    "Pellick began crossing Western Australia’s Rottnest Channel before her English Channel solo. In 1994 she swam from the mainland to Rottnest and back in 12 hours 6 minutes 12 seconds. The Rottnest Channel Swim Association inducted her into its Hall of Fame in 2015.",
    "The English Channel swim on 4 July 1995 took 12 hours 23 minutes. The Catalina federation records 11 hours 19 minutes 30 seconds on 11 August 2013. In New York the 17 June 2000 Manhattan circuit took 8 hours 15 minutes 50 seconds."
